{
 "about": "Settings opened and a setting changed with the keyboard alone (docs/adr/0039-keyboard-access.mdx): Allo (sample/EditingProbe.tsx) with the shell, the screen reader on in Spanish. Super+F2 puts the keyboard on the Oxy menu, Return opens it on System Settings and Return opens Settings; Settings opens at its own size, its sidebar beside the page; Tab reaches its search field, then the sidebar's selected row, and ↓ goes down the sidebar's one list to Accessibility, each row chosen, its page shown and said once with its ring; Tab reaches Reduce motion's switch and Space turns it on, the session telling every application; Shift+Tab goes back. Every step checks the keyboard's focus, what the assistive technology holds of Settings, what the reader says and what is announced. At 1.25 (1600 × 1000).",
 "locale": "es_ES.UTF-8",
 "module": "EditingProbe",
 "window": [
  600,
  360
